<title>INDIA: India Lloyds Steel 96/97 down 99 pct.</title>
<headline>India Lloyds Steel 96/97 down 99 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		8.2	vs     1,124.4</p>
<p>    Operating income  9,793.0	vs    12,611.8</p>
<p>    Other income	   37.8	vs	  62.6</p>
<p>    Gross profit	2,756.4	vs     2,206.5</p>
<p>    Interest	    1,243.6	vs     1,433.2</p>
<p>    Cash profit	 1,512.8	vs	 773.3</p>
<p>    Depreciation	  388.4	vs	 765.1</p>
<p>Note: Lloyds Steel Industries Ltd said production of hot-rolled coil steeel rose to 402,946 tonnes during the year compared to 380,477 tonnes a year ago.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite an increase in turnover and production levels, the company's bottomline has been drastically affected ...The cost of production at the plant has gone up due to a substantial increase in the input costs like power, administered price of coal, petroleum products and freight costs,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>It said the company is building a 80 MW power plant costing 3.94 billion rupees as a buffer against increasing power costs.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
